   var child = window.open();
   child.document.write('<h1>Hello</h1>');
   ```
2. 🐛 The new page opens but its document does not say `Hello`

### Summary

`TerminalInstance.sendText()` (reached via `runCommand`) calls `this.xterm?.scrollToBottom()`, which forwards to `XtermTerminal.scrollToBottom()` → bundled xterm.js `scrollToBottom` → `scrollLines` → `get dimensions`. When this runs against a terminal whose renderer has not been initialized yet (the xterm instance exists but `attachToElement`/`raw.open()` has not run, so the render service and its `dimensions` object do not exist), xterm.js throws `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'dimensions')`. 389 users / 448 hits across Windows, Mac, and Linux on 1.140.0.

Fixes microsoft/vscode\#339313
Recommended reviewer: ``@meganrogge``

### Culprit Commit

No single culprit commit — this is a **pre-existing latent race** that surfaced as a new stable bucket in 1.140.0. The entry path `sendText → scrollToBottom` (`terminalInstance.ts` line, authored 2022) and the `XtermTerminal.scrollToBottom` wrapper (authored 2021) both long predate the baseline, and `git blame` on the throwing call sites points to commits years older than the regression window. The anomaly is a timing/re-bucketing shift (bundled xterm.js scroll internals), not a logic change in a commit within the 1.139.1→1.140.0 range.

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Commit | Not identified — pre-existing |
| Author | n/a |
| PR | n/a |
| Message | n/a |
| Why | The crash path exists since 2021–2022; no commit in the regression window changes the triggering logic. Treated as a pre-existing boundary race. |

### Code Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Caller as runCommand / sendText
    participant Inst as TerminalInstance
    participant Xterm as XtermTerminal
    participant Raw as xterm.js (bundled)

    Caller->>Inst: sendText(text, shouldExecute)
    Inst->>Xterm: this.xterm?.scrollToBottom()
    Note over Xterm: ⚠️ Boundary: renderer not<br/>yet initialized (no attachToElement)
    Xterm->>Raw: this.raw.scrollToBottom()
    Raw->>Raw: scrollLines() -> get dimensions
    Note over Raw: 💥 TypeError: Cannot read<br/>properties of undefined (reading 'dimensions')
```

### Affected Files

| File | Role | Evidence |
|------|------|----------|
| `node_modules/@xterm/xterm/lib/xterm.js` | crash site | `get dimensions` (from stack) — bundled third-party, unmodifiable |
| `src/vs/workbench/contrib/terminal/browser/xterm/xtermTerminal.ts` | boundary / fix site | L767-L768: `scrollToBottom(): void { this.raw.scrollToBottom(); }` delegates straight into xterm.js with no attach guard |
| `src/vs/workbench/contrib/terminal/browser/terminalInstance.ts` | trigger | L1422: `this.xterm?.scrollToBottom();` inside `sendText`, which can run before the instance is attached to the DOM |

### Repro Steps

This is a timing-dependent race, so it is non-deterministic:

1. Trigger `sendText`/`runCommand` on a `TerminalInstance` whose xterm object has been created but not yet attached to the DOM (`attachToElement` / `raw.open()` not yet called) — e.g. programmatic command execution against a backgrounded or just-created terminal, or a restart that re-creates the xterm before re-attaching.
2. `sendText` reaches `this.xterm?.scrollToBottom()`.
3. xterm.js walks `scrollToBottom → scrollLines → get dimensions` and dereferences the render service's `dimensions`, which is `undefined` because the renderer was never opened.
4. `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'dimensions')` is thrown.

Increase likelihood by executing commands against terminals immediately on creation or during a restart, before layout/attach completes.

### How the Fix Works

**Chosen approach** (`src/vs/workbench/contrib/terminal/browser/xterm/xtermTerminal.ts`): Add an early-return guard `if (!this._attached) { return; }` to the renderer-delegating scroll wrappers (`scrollToBottom`, `scrollUpLine`, `scrollDownLine`, `scrollUpPage`, `scrollDownPage`, `scrollToTop`). `_attached` is set only after `attachToElement` runs `this.raw.open(container)` — the exact point at which xterm.js constructs its render service and the `dimensions` object the throwing code reads. The producer of the violating value is bundled third-party xterm.js, which cannot be modified in this repo, so the fix is placed at VS Code's own boundary wrapper and gated on the real lifecycle signal (`_attached`) rather than suppressing the symptom at the crash site. Scrolling a terminal that has no renderer yet is a no-op anyway, so the guard changes no user-visible behavior. The guard is not a `try/catch` and does not touch any `logService.error` path.

**Alternatives considered**:
- Wrapping the `scrollToBottom` call in `terminalInstance.sendText` in `try/catch` — rejected because it hides the error from telemetry instead of preventing the invalid lifecycle call, and would mask other legitimate failures.
- Optional-chaining into xterm.js internals (`this.raw.scrollToBottom?.()`) — rejected because the method is always callable; the undefined value is deep inside xterm.js's render service, unreachable from the wrapper, so chaining would not prevent the throw.

### Recommended Owner

``@meganrogge`` — terminal area owner; authored the `sendText → scrollToBottom` call path and is an active core maintainer with write access (commits within the last 90 days).

