`LanguageModelChatProvider` was finalized in #263415 (completing #250007). Two days later, #264061 added `statusIcon` to the `chatProvider` proposal, and it has stayed there ever since:

```ts
// vscode.proposed.chatProvider.d.ts
export interface LanguageModelChatInformation {
    // ...
    readonly statusIcon?: ThemeIcon;
}
```

([declaration](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/1f6488722c942d1d7528a7d949769a69e4a557c3/src/vscode-dts/vscode.proposed.chatProvider.d.ts#L79); all links below are pinned to `1f64887`)

Unlike its neighbours `isDefault` and `isUserSelectable`, it isn't marked "NOT BEING FINALIZED". Nothing seems to be tracking it, so I'd like to request finalization.

### Why it matters to extensions using only the stable API

`statusIcon` isn't just decoration. In the language models management editor, the stable [`tooltip`](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/1f6488722c942d1d7528a7d949769a69e4a557c3/src/vscode-dts/vscode.d.ts#L20604) property is only shown in a model's hover when `statusIcon` is also set: [`getModelHoverContent()`](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/1f6488722c942d1d7528a7d949769a69e4a557c3/src/vs/workbench/contrib/chat/browser/chatManagement/chatModelsWidget.ts#L72) and [`ModelNameColumnRenderer.renderModelElement()`](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/1f6488722c942d1d7528a7d949769a69e4a557c3/src/vs/workbench/contrib/chat/browser/chatManagement/chatModelsWidget.ts#L635) both check `statusIcon && tooltip`. Extensions on the stable API therefore can't show `tooltip` there at all, which works against how `tooltip` is documented in `vscode.d.ts`.

Where `statusIcon` is rendered today:
- Next to the selected model's name on the [chat input model picker button](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/1f6488722c942d1d7528a7d949769a69e4a557c3/src/vs/workbench/contrib/chat/browser/widget/input/modelPicker/modelPickerWidget.ts#L810-L814)
- As the item icon in the [model picker dropdown](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/1f6488722c942d1d7528a7d949769a69e4a557c3/src/vs/workbench/contrib/chat/browser/widget/input/modelPicker/modelPickerItemPrimitives.ts#L167)
- Next to the model name in the [language models management editor](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/1f6488722c942d1d7528a7d949769a69e4a557c3/src/vs/workbench/contrib/chat/browser/chatManagement/chatModelsWidget.ts#L618), and before the `tooltip` text in its [hover](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/1f6488722c942d1d7528a7d949769a69e4a557c3/src/vs/workbench/contrib/chat/browser/chatManagement/chatModelsWidget.ts#L72-L78)

### Use case

**First-party precedent.** Copilot Chat already depends on this. When a model has a warning, [`languageModelAccess.ts`](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/1f6488722c942d1d7528a7d949769a69e4a557c3/extensions/copilot/src/extension/conversation/vscode-node/languageModelAccess.ts#L353-L354) puts the warning in `tooltip` and [sets a warning `statusIcon`](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/1f6488722c942d1d7528a7d949769a69e4a557c3/extensions/copilot/src/extension/conversation/vscode-node/languageModelAccess.ts#L397):

```ts
if (warnings?.rowWarning) {
    modelTooltip = warnings.rowWarning;
}
// ...
tooltip: modelTooltip,
statusIcon: warnings?.rowWarning ? new vscode.ThemeIcon('warning') : undefined,
```

So the API's shape and its UI have already been used in production by the main provider. Only third-party providers are locked out.

**Third-party providers have the same need.** BYOK, proxy, gateway and self-hosted providers all front upstream services whose health changes at runtime: outages, rate limiting, exhausted quota, expired credentials, deprecated or retiring models. The best place to warn users is the model picker, before they send a request that will fail or be slow. Today a stable-API provider can only:

- leave the model as is and let requests fail, or
- hide it with `isUserSelectable: false` (also proposed), so it disappears without explanation, or
- put the status into `name`/`detail` (e.g. "GPT-X (degraded)"), which breaks the model's identity in the picker and in settings.

Sample, following the same pattern as Copilot:

```ts
class GatewayChatProvider implements vscode.LanguageModelChatProvider {
    private readonly _onDidChange = new vscode.EventEmitter<void>();
    readonly onDidChangeLanguageModelChatInformation = this._onDidChange.event;

    constructor(private readonly gateway: GatewayClient) {
        gateway.onDidChangeHealth(() => this._onDidChange.fire());
    }

    async provideLanguageModelChatInformation(_options: { silent: boolean }, token: vscode.CancellationToken) {
        const models = await this.gateway.listModels(token);
        return models.map(m => {
            const status = this.gateway.health(m.id); // 'ok' | 'degraded' | 'quotaExhausted' | 'deprecated'
            return {
                id: m.id,
                name: m.displayName,
                family: m.family,
                version: m.version,
                maxInputTokens: m.maxInput,
                maxOutputTokens: m.maxOutput,
                capabilities: { toolCalling: m.supportsTools, imageInput: m.supportsVision },
                statusIcon: statusToIcon(status),
                tooltip: statusToMessage(m, status),
            } satisfies vscode.LanguageModelChatInformation;
        });
    }

    // provideLanguageModelChatResponse / provideTokenCount omitted
}

function statusToIcon(status: ModelHealth): vscode.ThemeIcon | undefined {
    switch (status) {
        case 'degraded': return new vscode.ThemeIcon('warning');
        case 'quotaExhausted': return new vscode.ThemeIcon('error');
        case 'deprecated': return new vscode.ThemeIcon('info');
        default: return undefined;
    }
}
```

When health changes, the provider fires `onDidChangeLanguageModelChatInformation`, so the picker and management editor update without the user reopening anything.

