`DocumentUnicodeHighlighter._update()` sends `computedUnicodeHighlights` to the editor worker. When the promise resolves it checks only that the model is not disposed and that its version did not change, then calls `this._decorations.set(...)`:

https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/5e418d6d41f7464a64877411e8ae3b20669d5c71/src/vs/editor/contrib/unicodeHighlighter/browser/unicodeHighlighter.ts#L243-L279

`UnicodeHighlighter._updateHighlighter()` disposes the highlighter whenever the options change, for example when the model's language switches to one whose `[language]` settings turn the highlighting off. If that happens while the request is in flight, `dispose()` clears the collection and the late result then fills it again. Nothing references that collection any more, so the boxes stay until the model is detached from the editor (switching tabs). Text typed afterwards is not boxed, because the live highlighter has the right options.

Where users hit it: an editor restored at window start is `plaintext` until extension contributions are processed. In Restricted Mode its highlighter has `nonBasicASCII` on and sends a request. Then the language switches to one whose extension contributes, say, `"[ktav]": { "editor.unicodeHighlight.nonBasicASCII": false }`. If the worker has not answered yet, every non-ASCII character in the file keeps its box for the whole session.

Steps to reproduce (the large diff keeps the single editor worker busy, so the request is still in flight when the language changes):

1. User settings: `"[markdown]": { "editor.unicodeHighlight.nonBasicASCII": false }`. Open a folder in Restricted Mode.
2. Open `b.md` containing `ключ: значение §`. No boxes.
3. From an extension (`activationEvents: ["onLanguage:markdown"]`), with `big-a.txt` and `big-b.txt` two ~1 MB files that differ in about 30% of 60 000 lines:

```js
const vscode = require("vscode");
const sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));
exports.activate = async () => {
  await sleep(5000);
  const ed = vscode.window.visibleTextEditors.find((e) => e.document.languageId === "markdown");
  void vscode.commands.executeCommand("vscode.diff", BIG_A_URI, BIG_B_URI, "big",
    { viewColumn: vscode.ViewColumn.Two, preserveFocus: true });
  await sleep(800);
  await vscode.languages.setTextDocumentLanguage(ed.document, "plaintext");
  await sleep(700);
  await vscode.languages.setTextDocumentLanguage(ed.document, "markdown");
};
```

4. When the diff finishes, every non-ASCII character in `b.md` is boxed, although `markdown` has `nonBasicASCII: false`. A line typed now gets no box. The boxes go away only after switching to another tab and back.

Suggested fix: drop the result once the highlighter is disposed, e.g. `if (this._store.isDisposed) { return; }` at the top of the `.then` callback, or cancel it with a `CancellationTokenSource` disposed in `dispose()`.

